{
 "description": "Parity case class (#1640 review F1 round 3): the oracle's is_ratelimit greps only gh's stderr for `secondary rate limit|(http )?429|too many requests`, so the verb decides on the same text — the forge's status line, message and errors[] items — and on nothing else. THE VERB'S OWN TEXT: gh's stderr never carries the repo slug or the request's host:port, so a `429` that appears only in the verb's own error text (here the repo name, which the verb's REST path and a transport error both quote) must never stop the cycle — neither for an HTTP failure nor for a connection that drops before any answer.",
